cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these designs or SFC profile 2.0, please cite this deposit and the framework paper listed under references."
title: "Sustainability-First Distributed Ledger Systems: Six Reference Designs and SFC Profile 2.0"
abstract: >-
  Six original distributed-ledger system designs addressing ecological challenges in supply-chain
  certification, healthcare and pharmacy interchange, paperless billing, recycling and material
  recovery, cross-operator roaming, and carbon-credit MRV. All six follow SFC profile 2.0, one
  Sustainability-First Consensus engineering profile that turns sustainability criteria into checkable properties: an
  annual energy budget, hardware-lifecycle constraints, signed on-chain energy and carbon attestations
  with an offset-coverage rule (a narrowed reading of the framework's Net Zero criterion, not a net-zero claim), disclosure through the sustainability-data
  well-known URI with an evidence-to-disclosure bridge, and a platform rule with a public case (public energy
  assessment) and a permissioned case (the deployment's own energy check or a registered-node bound). All work is documented at design level; no system is implemented or deployed.
